From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:29:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 41/72] hottyterm: stage stamps for the latency rig
 (HOTTY_TRACE)

With HOTTY_TRACE=<dir>, the terminal writes hottyterm-<pid>.jsonl in the
trace format hotty/1 (hottyterm's docs/trace.md): one line per stage on
the shared monotonic clock. The stages are the key and pointer events,
the pty's reads and writes, each parsed batch and hotty command,
hotty-blitz's rendering, the renderer's draw and upload, and the frame on
its way to the screen: on Linux, GTK's frame clock taking it; on macOS,
the display link's tick, the IOSurface handed to the main thread, and
the main thread setting the layer's contents. Off, a stamp is one atomic
load and a branch.

The writer is in hotty.zig. Upstream files get hooks: the input
callbacks' lock sites in Surface.zig go through one function, a few
lines in termio/Exec.zig, renderer/generic.zig,
renderer/metal/IOSurfaceLayer.zig and apprt/gtk/class/surface.zig, and
the frame clock's in apprt/gtk/class/render_surface.zig.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
